00:08:49.120 --> 00:08:51.320
And it's probably just
gonna go (beep) after this.

00:08:51.320 --> 00:08:52.950
(all laughing)

00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:54.320
- No, it's not wait,

00:08:54.320 --> 00:08:56.100
but this is amazing 'cause
you also worked with

00:08:56.100 --> 00:08:57.769
Sir Paul McCartney on this
record, that's amazing.

00:08:57.769 --> 00:08:58.602
- Yeah.

00:08:58.602 --> 00:08:59.893
- Did he produce you?

00:08:59.893 --> 00:09:01.050
- Is that what it-

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:02.392
He produced, yeah.

00:09:02.392 --> 00:09:03.937
- What, it was that conversation like,

00:09:03.937 --> 00:09:05.720
"Hi, sir."

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:06.720
- It was,

00:09:06.720 --> 00:09:08.250
yeah, will you produce, will you come?

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:09.680
And there was a song that,

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:11.240
it was a great song that he wrote

00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:12.940
and I asked him if he would produce.

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:14.330
And he said yes.

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:16.200
And I got very quiet on the phone.

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:18.070
And he thought he, he had lost me

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:19.717
and he said,

00:09:19.717 --> 00:09:20.550
"Hello?"

00:09:20.550 --> 00:09:21.460
this is really true too.

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:22.990
He said, "Hello, hello?

00:09:22.990 --> 00:09:24.250
And I said "Hi."

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:26.010
And he said, "Oh, I thought I lost you."

00:09:26.010 --> 00:09:26.860
And I said, "no."

00:09:26.860 --> 00:09:28.617
I said, "I just pooped my pants."

00:09:29.950 --> 00:09:30.783
- I'll be right back.

00:09:30.783 --> 00:09:31.860
- Because I was like, what the,

00:09:31.860 --> 00:09:32.890
this is happening.

00:09:32.890 --> 00:09:34.450
And, this whole record was...

00:09:34.450 --> 00:09:35.500
I mean, Willie Nelson.

00:09:35.500 --> 00:09:37.100
I mean, he's my hero dude.

00:09:37.100 --> 00:09:39.690
And get to sing crazy with Willie and,

00:09:39.690 --> 00:09:40.523
get to write-

00:09:40.523 --> 00:09:42.337
- What did the studio smell like?

00:09:42.337 --> 00:09:44.020
(all laughing)

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:45.870
- I don't remember, I don't remember.

00:09:45.870 --> 00:09:47.150
- What was one of your favorites though,

00:09:47.150 --> 00:09:48.260
to do on the record?

00:09:48.260 --> 00:09:50.940
- I think "Higher" was
easily, one of my...

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:52.473
This is weird, but my,

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:55.150
one of the title tracks, "Higher",

00:09:55.150 --> 00:09:57.858
Was co-written by my eight year old.

00:09:57.858 --> 00:09:58.691
- Oh

00:09:58.691 --> 00:09:59.570
- Yeah, he came into,

00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:01.080
I was giving the kids a shower

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:02.617
and doing the shampoo
and stuff and he said,

00:10:02.617 --> 00:10:03.780
"Poppy, I wrote a song."

00:10:03.780 --> 00:10:04.613
and I said, go for it.

00:10:04.613 --> 00:10:05.900
And he said,

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:07.369
♪ When you go low ♪

00:10:07.369 --> 00:10:08.964
♪ and I'd go high, ♪

00:10:08.964 --> 00:10:10.497
♪ dun dun dun ♪

00:10:10.497 --> 00:10:11.950
And I said like, this
is good. Like, really?

00:10:11.950 --> 00:10:15.510
And then I thought, "Did
you hear that on YouTube?"

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:16.720
I freaked out
- Scouring.

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:18.340
I was like, "Where did
you hear that, honey?"

00:10:18.340 --> 00:10:19.397
He said like, "No, no, I wrote it."

00:10:19.397 --> 00:10:21.140
And I said, but really?

00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:22.900
- Yeah, what show were you watching?

00:10:22.900 --> 00:10:25.356
- And then I sat with
Ryan tater and Greg Wells

00:10:25.356 --> 00:10:26.189
and we were,

00:10:26.189 --> 00:10:27.625
on a writing session, yeah

00:10:27.625 --> 00:10:28.540
And I said,

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:29.373
I panicked.

00:10:29.373 --> 00:10:30.524
And I said,

00:10:30.524 --> 00:10:31.720
"Hey, can I sing this song
my eight year old...?"

00:10:31.720 --> 00:10:33.960
And I sang it and they were
like, "This is really good."

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:35.290
And then we came up with this song,

00:10:35.290 --> 00:10:37.120
and now it's happening.

00:10:37.120 --> 00:10:38.350
And I did a,

00:10:38.350 --> 00:10:40.500
my son is gonna be rich.

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:42.063
- How cool is that though?

00:10:42.063 --> 00:10:43.478
That you did it,

00:10:43.478 --> 00:10:45.153
that's so cool.

00:10:45.153 --> 00:10:45.986
I love we're such a...

00:10:45.986 --> 00:10:48.100
You do turn into like a mush
pot when you become a parent.

00:10:48.100 --> 00:10:49.336
Cause you're like,

00:10:49.336 --> 00:10:50.350
how can I involve my
children in my projects?

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:51.510
- I didn't mean to honestly

00:10:51.510 --> 00:10:52.760
and even after that writing session

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:56.305
I came home and I kept
saying, are you sure?

00:10:56.305 --> 00:10:57.820
'Cause, then I was really panicking

00:10:57.820 --> 00:10:59.250
and he went to the piano,

00:10:59.250 --> 00:11:00.550
and he said, "no, look."

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:02.996
And he went,(making piano sound)

00:11:02.996 --> 00:11:03.829
- I love that.

00:11:03.829 --> 00:11:04.662
- Yeah, it's amazing, yeah

00:11:04.662 --> 00:11:06.200
- But it's so fun to see your kid, like,

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:07.180
'cause we love art

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:09.590
and it's like our therapy
and it's like our bloodline.

00:11:09.590 --> 00:11:10.790
So like it's like in us.

00:11:10.790 --> 00:11:11.623
- I always say this.

00:11:11.623 --> 00:11:12.563
Like it is,

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:14.453
People often come to me,

00:11:14.453 --> 00:11:15.286
I'm sure they do to you.

00:11:15.286 --> 00:11:16.119
And they'll say like,

00:11:16.119 --> 00:11:17.910
"Oh my son or my daughter,

00:11:17.910 --> 00:11:19.370
they want to do this."

00:11:19.370 --> 00:11:21.520
And I'll always say to them, listen,

00:11:21.520 --> 00:11:22.680
they are so blessed.

00:11:22.680 --> 00:11:24.740
The gift of the romance with music

00:11:24.740 --> 00:11:26.310
is the greatest romance I'll ever.

00:11:26.310 --> 00:11:29.178
No man, no woman will ever break their-

00:11:29.178 --> 00:11:30.777
- The relationship that
won't let you down.

00:11:30.777 --> 00:11:31.610
- You will always have that,

00:11:31.610 --> 00:11:33.690
and it is the deepest, most purest level.

00:11:33.690 --> 00:11:34.523
Like when I hear music,

00:11:34.523 --> 00:11:36.500
it is like the voice of God speaking, so,

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:37.990
- Yeah.

00:11:37.990 --> 00:11:39.050
I'm so happy for you for this record.

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:39.883
That's so cool.

00:11:39.883 --> 00:11:40.716
- Thank you so much.

00:11:40.716 --> 00:11:41.549
I know that feeling,

00:11:41.549 --> 00:11:43.110
of like making something you're,

00:11:43.110 --> 00:11:45.150
truly proud of every part of it.

00:11:45.150 --> 00:11:47.030
- Obviously I'm proud of
my other records, but it's,

00:11:47.030 --> 00:11:48.675
- Me too, but there are
ones that are special.

00:11:48.675 --> 00:11:50.880
- It's been a while since
I've written songs like this

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:51.713
and gone like,

00:11:51.713 --> 00:11:53.680
"Oh my God, I think
I'm gonna have a hits".

00:11:53.680 --> 00:11:55.084
- I love that feeling.

00:11:55.084 --> 00:11:55.917
- That's a weird feeling.

00:11:55.917 --> 00:11:56.890
Yeah, yeah, And it feels good.

00:11:56.890 --> 00:11:58.660
Yeah, especially when you step out of

00:11:58.660 --> 00:11:59.550
being like a parent

00:11:59.550 --> 00:12:01.070
and you're like, wait, this is what I do.

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:01.903
- Totally.

00:12:01.903 --> 00:12:02.736
This is like, yeah.

00:12:02.736 --> 00:12:03.620
You're like, I'm cool, wait.

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:06.070
So wait, you're performing a song today,

00:12:06.070 --> 00:12:08.296
and it's called, "I'll
never not love you."

00:12:08.296 --> 00:12:09.129
- "I'll Never not Love You."

00:12:09.129 --> 00:12:10.760
What's that about, other
than never not loving them.

00:12:10.760 --> 00:12:12.411
- I think it's about the greatest,

00:12:12.411 --> 00:12:13.500
I think it's about the gift,

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:15.850
The greatest gift you
can ever give or receive.

00:12:17.485 --> 00:12:19.100
And when my mom had us and we were little,

00:12:19.100 --> 00:12:21.290
she used to tell us over and over again,

00:12:21.290 --> 00:12:23.150
that unconditional love
was the greatest thing

00:12:23.150 --> 00:12:24.650
you could ever give anybody.

00:12:24.650 --> 00:12:27.110
And so I think that's
what the song is about.

00:12:27.110 --> 00:12:29.390
I think it's about all
of us have been hurt.

00:12:29.390 --> 00:12:31.820
All of us have been put in a
place where we're vulnerable

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:33.860
and we're scared to go through it again.

00:12:33.860 --> 00:12:36.520
And this is me saying to that person,

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:38.620
listen, fall into me, trust me.

00:12:38.620 --> 00:12:39.500
And,

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:40.435
it's not gonna happen again

00:12:40.435 --> 00:12:41.268
- Fall Into me.

00:12:41.268 --> 00:12:42.300
Okay sir.

00:12:42.300 --> 00:12:43.850
That's a nice line.

00:12:43.850 --> 00:12:45.153
That's a nice line.

